post 1 "Minimal Adaptive Card"        "$T1" yes ""
post 2 "Alert-shaped Adaptive Card"   "$T2" yes ""
post 3 "Legacy MessageCard"           "$T3" yes "Legacy payloads drop in unchanged -- useful for Grafana and old scripts."
post 4 "Raw Azure Monitor payload"    "$T4" no  "This is why you need a transform between the action group and this URL."

hr
printf 'Passed: %s   Failed: %s\n' "$PASS" "$FAIL"
hr
cat <<'NOTES'

How to read the results
-----------------------
Test 1 fails
  Nothing else matters. Check: flow is turned On; trigger auth is "Anyone" and
  you sent no Authorization header; URL copied whole (it is long and the sig
  query param is easy to truncate); egress from this host reaches
  *.logic.azure.us.

Test 1 passes, nothing appears in Teams
  The trigger accepted the POST but the post action failed. Open the flow's
  run history in the maker portal. In a gov tenant the overwhelmingly likely
  cause is "Post as" still set to Flow Bot -- look for
  BotNotInConversationRoster. Change it to User.

Test 2 fails but Test 1 passed
  Your card expression is wrong. The Adaptive Card field should be
  @{triggerBody()?['attachments'][0]['content']}, not the whole trigger body.

Test 3 passes
  Good news: anything already emitting MessageCards works with a URL swap.
  Note that buttons in MessageCards will not render under Workflows.

Test 4 fails with 400
  Expected and correct. Azure Monitor's common alert schema is not a card
  schema. Put a Consumption Logic App in Azure Gov between the action group
  and this URL to build the card. Test 2's payload is the target shape.

Test 4 unexpectedly passes
  Check what actually landed in the channel -- it is probably an empty or
  malformed card. Still needs the transform.

NOTES
